1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,740
The bank turned five grand of debt into twelve fucking thousand.

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:07,180
And all you did was pay the minimum, like they told you.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,520
Here's the setup: you owe five thousand on a card at about twenty-two percent.

4
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:14,480
The minimum is the tiniest payment they'll let you make.

5
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:18,380
Month one, you pay a hundred forty-three bucks, and your debt drops just fifty.

6
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:23,060
The rest is interest, aka the bank's tip for being a bank.

7
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:25,820
Double-tap if your card has ever done you dirty.

8
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:31,580
And here's the shitty part. As your balance shrinks, the minimum shrinks too, so you crawl.

9
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,040
Five years later? You still owe about twenty-seven hundred dollars.

10
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:38,400
That's more than half the original debt, still sitting there.

11
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,220
Send this to whoever's been paying the minimum since college.

12
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:45,240
So when are you free? Sixteen and a half damn years.

13
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:48,300
A baby born that day could be getting a driver's license.

14
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,100
Follow, 'cause the total? It's disgusting.

15
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:56,520
You paid twelve thousand eight hundred eleven dollars for five grand of stuff you don't even remember.

16
00:00:56,520 --> 00:01:00,460
Paying a flat two fifty a month would've killed it in twenty-six months.

17
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:03,820
That's fourteen years faster, with the exact same card.

18
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,100
Minimum or flat? One word.

